1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,765
The urn was supposed to hold diamonds.
It held a receipt dated six minutes

2
00:00:05,765 --> 00:00:07,000
into the future.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,353
Jason called it a joke until Lucia found
the delivery slot, still warm

4
00:00:12,353 --> 00:00:14,000
inside the cold warehouse.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,941
A courier had scanned the wrong package
early. Somewhere behind that wall,

6
00:00:18,941 --> 00:00:21,000
their diamonds were still waiting.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,667
They followed a grinding belt toward a
kiln, where rejected packages were

8
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:28,000
dropped directly into the firing
chamber.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,667
Jason reached for the emergency stop.
Lucia caught his wrist. The stop

10
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,000
switch also opened the disposal hatch.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,667
She fed the orange receipt through the
reader instead. The belt reversed

12
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:42,000
to correct its own failed delivery.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,765
The sealed urn rolled back to Jason,
heavy this time. He bagged it without

14
00:00:47,765 --> 00:00:49,000
opening the lid.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,118
Their receipt showed one successful
collection. The kiln's furnace log

16
00:00:53,118 --> 00:00:56,000
showed nothing missing, because nothing
had burned.
